.* definitions and command/sys-cpps/help/; do not edit.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CHGGRPA.Change Group Attributes (CHGGRPA)
:P.Use the Change Group Attributes (CHGGRPA) command to make the job a
group job, rename it, or leave the group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGGRPA/GRPJOB'.Group job (GRPJOB)
:P.The group job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGGRPA/GRPJOBTXT'.Group job text (GRPJOBTXT)
:P.The group job text for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGGRPA/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.No message queue&colon. messages are not sent.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTIMZON.Change Time Zone Description (CHGTIMZON)
:P.Use the Change Time Zone Description (CHGTIMZON) command to change a
time zone description in QSYS. When the description is the one the
QTIMZON system value names, the system's local time and QUTCOFFSET
follow the change at once.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/TIMZON'.Time zone description (TIMZON)
:P.The time zone description to change.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/OFFSET'.Offset (OFFSET)
:P.The difference between standard time in the zone and UTC, in minutes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from -779 to 779.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/STDNAME'.Standard Time (STDNAME)
:P.The abbreviated and full names of standard time.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Abbreviated name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Full name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/DSTNAME'.Daylight Saving Time (DST) (DSTNAME)
:P.The abbreviated and full names of daylight saving time; *NONE removes
daylight saving time from the zone.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Abbreviated name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Full name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/STDMSG'.Standard Time message (STDMSG)
:P.The message that holds the names of standard time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/DSTMSG'.DST message (DSTMSG)
:P.The message that holds the names of daylight saving time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file of the messages.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/DSTSTR'.Daylight Saving Time start (DSTSTR)
:P.When daylight saving time starts.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JAN, *FEB, *MAR, *APR, *MAY, *JUN, *AUG, *SEP,
*OCT, *NOV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Day
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU, *FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Relative day of month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 3, 4.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/DSTEND'.Daylight Saving Time end (DSTEND)
:P.When daylight saving time ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JAN, *FEB, *MAR, *APR, *MAY, *JUN, *AUG, *SEP,
*OCT, *NOV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Day
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU, *FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Relative day of month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 3, 4.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/DSTSHIFT'.Daylight Saving Time shift (DSTSHIFT)
:P.How many minutes the clock moves forward when daylight saving time
starts.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 120.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A description of the time zone description.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/YEAROFS'.Year offset (YEAROFS)
:P.The number of years added to the Gregorian year.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from -140 to 140.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTIMZON/ALTNAME'.Alternate name (ALTNAME)
:P.Another name for the zone.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTTIMZON.Create Time Zone Description (CRTTIMZON)
:P.Use the Create Time Zone Description (CRTTIMZON) command to create a
time zone description in library QSYS&colon. an offset from UTC, the
names of standard and daylight saving time and the rule that starts and
ends daylight saving time. The QTIMZON system value names the
description the system's local time follows.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/TIMZON'.Time zone description (TIMZON)
:P.The name of the time zone description to create. It is created in
QSYS.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/OFFSET'.Offset (OFFSET)
:P.The difference between standard time in the zone and UTC, in
minutes&colon. negative west of Greenwich, positive east of it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from -779 to 779.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/STDNAME'.Standard Time (STDNAME)
:P.The abbreviated and full names of standard time. *GEN makes the
abbreviation from the offset; *MSG takes both names from the message
STDMSG names.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Abbreviated name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Full name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/DSTNAME'.Daylight Saving Time (DST) (DSTNAME)
:P.The abbreviated and full names of daylight saving time. *NONE means
the zone keeps no daylight saving time; *MSG takes both names from the
message DSTMSG names.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Abbreviated name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Full name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/STDMSG'.Standard Time message (STDMSG)
:P.The message that holds the names of standard time when STDNAME(*MSG)
is given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/DSTMSG'.DST message (DSTMSG)
:P.The message that holds the names of daylight saving time when
DSTNAME(*MSG) is given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file of STDMSG and DSTMSG.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCPFMSG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/DSTSTR'.Daylight Saving Time start (DSTSTR)
:P.When daylight saving time starts&colon. the month, the day of the
week, which of those days in the month (the first to the fourth, or the
last) and the local standard time.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JAN, *FEB, *MAR, *APR, *MAY, *JUN, *AUG, *SEP,
*OCT, *NOV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Day
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU, *FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Relative day of month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 3, 4.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/DSTEND'.Daylight Saving Time end (DSTEND)
:P.When daylight saving time ends&colon. the month, the day of the week,
which of those days in the month and the local daylight saving time.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JAN, *FEB, *MAR, *APR, *MAY, *JUN, *AUG, *SEP,
*OCT, *NOV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Day
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU, *FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Relative day of month
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 3, 4.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/DSTSHIFT'.Daylight Saving Time shift (DSTSHIFT)
:P.How many minutes the clock moves forward when daylight saving time
starts.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 120.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 60 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A description of the time zone description.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/YEAROFS'.Year offset (YEAROFS)
:P.The number of years added to the Gregorian year when the zone's dates
are shown.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from -140 to 140.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/ALTNAME'.Alternate name (ALTNAME)
:P.Another name for the zone, such as the name the IANA time zone
database gives it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTIMZON/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public has to the time zone description.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTTIMZON.Delete Time Zone Description (DLTTIMZON)
:P.Use the Delete Time Zone Description (DLTTIMZON) command to delete
time zone descriptions from QSYS. The description the QTIMZON system
value names cannot be deleted.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTTIMZON/TIMZON'.Time zone description (TIMZON)
:P.The time zone description to delete, or a generic name for every
description that starts with it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPWSUSR.Display Work Station User (DSPWSUSR)
:P.The Display Work Station User (DSPWSUSR) command works with the
display station and the jobs signed on at it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPWSUSR/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDGRPJOB.End Group Job (ENDGRPJOB)
:P.Use the End Group Job (ENDGRPJOB) command to end a job of the group,
or this one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDGRPJOB/GRPJOB'.Group job (GRPJOB)
:P.The group job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDGRPJOB/RSPGRPJOB'.Group job to be resumed (RSPGRPJOB)
:P.The group job to be resumed for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDGRPJOB/LOG'.Job log (LOG)
:P.The job log for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SETATNPGM.Set Attention Program (SETATNPGM)
:P.Use the Set Attention Program (SETATNPGM) command to set the program
the Attention key runs for the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETATNPGM/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETATNPGM/SET'.Set attention key (SET)
:P.The set attention key for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ON:EPK.
:PD.On.
:PT.:PK.*OFF:EPK.
:PD.Off.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TFRGRPJOB.Transfer to Group Job (TFRGRPJOB)
:P.Use the Transfer to Group Job (TFRGRPJOB) command to move the display
to another job of the group, starting it when the group has none of that
name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TFRGRPJOB/GRPJOB'.Group job (GRPJOB)
:P.The group job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TFRGRPJOB/INLGRPPGM'.Initial group program (INLGRPPGM)
:P.The initial group program for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TFRSECJOB.Transfer Secondary Job (TFRSECJOB)
:P.Use the Transfer Secondary Job (TFRSECJOB) command to move the
display to the secondary job, signing one on when there is none.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKTIMZON.Work with Time Zone Desc (WRKTIMZON)
:P.Use the Work with Time Zone Descriptions (WRKTIMZON) command to show
the time zone descriptions in QSYS and change, delete, display or print
them, or make one the system's time zone. The description the QTIMZON
system value names is marked with a greater-than sign.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKTIMZON/TIMZON'.Time zone description (TIMZON)
:P.The time zone descriptions to show&colon. a name, a generic name, or
*ALL.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
